        <p:txBody>
          <a:bodyPr>
            <a:normAutofit fontScale="92500"/>
          </a:bodyPr>
          <a:lstStyle/>
          <a:p>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Decoupled data and metadata between database and publication</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:pPr lvl="1"/>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Both data and metadata are reported in publications, while databases focus more on capturing complete datasets than complete metadata.</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:pPr lvl="1"/>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Issue: Difficulty in data quality evaluation and reproducibility by database users</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Inconsistent metadata reporting standards</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:pPr lvl="1"/>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Databases and publishers all have different metadata reporting requirements;</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:pPr lvl="1"/>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>General standards are often too broad, while specified standards are too few.</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:pPr lvl="1"/>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Issue: Inconsistent metadata reporting standards.</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Not in machine-readable or AI-ready formats</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:pPr lvl="1"/>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Metadata is usually reported in tables, footnotes, or natural language descriptions in the main text.</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:pPr lvl="1"/>
            <a:r>
              <a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
              <a:t>Issue: Incompatibility with machine-readable and AI-ready workflows.</a:t>
            </a:r>
          </a:p>
          <a:p>
            <a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/>
